{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "53", "x": 0.9032117274603759, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.03053152114325986, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "C", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.02101269433220525, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Tasks that are emotionally loaded or difficult, such as preparing for exams,", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.7661275853333133, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "are prime candidates for procrastination. People with low self-esteem are more", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.15152541916388573, "w": 0.8266932790689258, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "likely to procrastinate. Another group of people who tend to procrastinate are", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.17970752416545568, "w": 0.8261206772019258, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "perfectionists, who worry their work will be judged harshly by others. We know", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2080378742395933, "w": 0.826679540725116, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "that if we don't finish that report or complete those home repairs, then what we", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.23636822431373095, "w": 0.8258813839597454, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "did can't be evaluated. When we avoid such tasks, we also avoid the negative", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.26469857438786853, "w": 0.8260121032758466, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "emotions associated with them. This is rewarding, and it conditions us to use", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2930660423122369, "w": 0.826011898225939, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "procrastination to repair our mood. If we engage in more enjoyable tasks instead,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.32139637352567824, "w": 0.82598093568989, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "we get another mood boost. In the long run, however, procrastination isn't an", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3497267990426009, "w": 0.8261858830725457, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "effective way of managing emotions. The 'mood repair' we experience is", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3780571491167385, "w": 0.8260551637564446, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "temporary. Afterwards, people tend to be left with a sense of guilt that not only", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.40638753691226864, "w": 0.8263159872389241, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "increases their negative mood, but also reinforces their tendency to procrastinate.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4347178869864063, "w": 0.8268583442445515, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "D", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.47301087175797835, "w": 0.02101269433220525, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "So why is this such a problem? When most people think of the costs of", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.47301087175797835, "w": 0.7656221373110554, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "procrastination, they think of the toll on productivity. For example, studies have", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5013412218321159, "w": 0.8265155007990282, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "shown that procrastination negatively impacts on student performance. But", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5295232891122934, "w": 0.8261859855974996, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "putting off reading textbooks and writing essays may affect other areas of", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.557853639186431, "w": 0.8260117957009852, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "students' lives. In one study of over 3,000 German students over a six-month", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5861840269819611, "w": 0.8267433112463826, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "period, those who reported procrastinating over their university work were also", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6145143770560988, "w": 0.8260988393867654, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "more likely to engage in study-related misconduct, such as cheating and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6428448025730215, "w": 0.8264069268729489, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "plagiarism. But the behaviour that procrastination was most closely linked with", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6712121950546047, "w": 0.8261642503072929, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "was using fraudulent excuses to get deadline extensions. Other research shows", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6995426205715274, "w": 0.8262289435531438, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "that employees on average spend almost a quarter of their workday", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.727872970645665, "w": 0.8262295587028666, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "procrastinating, and again this is linked with negative outcomes. In fact, in one US", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7562033207198027, "w": 0.8262948670984402, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "survey of over 22,000 employees, participants who said they regularly", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7845337462367252, "w": 0.8265655329764849, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "procrastinated had less annual income and less employment stability. For every", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8128640963108629, "w": 0.8266449898156837, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "one-point increase on a measure of chronic procrastination, annual income", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8411944463850005, "w": 0.8261554331612657, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "decreased by US$15,000.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8695495416926252, "w": 0.2649588008599383, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "E", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.90766949843675, "w": 0.01919854090586743, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Procrastination also correlates with serious health and well-being", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.90766949843675, "w": 0.7663174615477598, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "problems. A tendency to procrastinate is linked to poor mental health, including", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9359998485108877, "w": 0.8260337360410994, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}